lementary --link between=SU-01,SU-02 --link triggered=EM-4`.\n4. Find what neither map shows alone:\n   - `genome graph cycles --across of`: loops that run through both people. A\'s withdrawal triggers B\'s\n     pursuit, which triggers A\'s withdrawal. This is the interlocking cycle to name as a `pattern`.\n   - `genome graph bridges --across of`: the single link carrying a whole dynamic. Change it and the dynamic\n     changes, so it is the leverage point.\n   - `genome graph hubs --across of`: the entries most entangled across the maps.\n   - `genome graph gaps --across of`: an entry of A and an entry of B that share neighbours but were never\n     linked. Offer it as a question, never as a finding.\n5. Name a pattern only with the operator: `genome new pattern --title "pursue-withdraw" --set type=pursue-withdraw\n   --link involves=SU-01,SU-02 --link sustained_by=PR-3,PR-9`. Interrupting and transforming it need evidence;\n   transforming is human-only.\n\n**Third parties.** People in this map did not consent to being modelled unless `consent=given`. Keep the map\nlocal (`privacy = "local"`; `close` refuses with a git remote). Never quote it to the person as fact.\n\'\'\'\n\n[kinds.subject]\npath = "map/subjects"\nid = "SU-{n:02}"\nfields = { role = "enum:self|partner|parent|child|sibling|friend|colleague|client|other!", attachment = "enum:secure|anxious|avoidant|disorganized|unknown", attachment_source = "enum:self-report|assessment|inferred|unknown", consent = "enum:self|given|not-asked|declined" }\n\n[kinds.bond]\npath = "map/bonds"\nid = "BO-{n:03}"\nfields = { dynamic = "enum:secure|anxious-avoidant|anxious-anxious|avoidant-avoidant|disorganized|mixed|unknown", safety = "int:0..10" }\n[kinds.bond.relations]\nbetween = { to = "subject", min = 2, max = 2, graph = false, inverse = "bond" }\nseen_by = { to = "subject", min = 1, max = 1, graph = false, default = "SU-01", inverse = "perceives" }\n\n[kinds.transaction]\npath = "map/transactions.jsonl"\nstore = "js